The only valid configuration occurs when vertices are placed as follows: \(A = (0,0)\), \(E = (20,0)\), \(B = (0,-b)\) with \(b > 14\), \(C = (14, 14-b)\), and \(D = (20, 8-b)\). Here \(AB = b\) is an integer, and the area of pentagon \(ABCDE\) is \(20b - 164\).

The area must be a multiple of \(16\), so \(20b - 164 \equiv 0 \pmod{16}\). Simplifying gives \(b \equiv 1 \pmod{4}\). Additionally, \(b > 14\) and \(b < 2026\). The smallest such \(b\) is \(17\), and the largest is \(2025\). The number of integers of the form \(4k+1\) in this range is \(503\).

\boxed{503}
